jobs.job:
The person is writing a page in Trillion's Write and asked you, right where they are writing: {ask}
How they want you to write: {instructions}
The page's title: {title}
What the page says before that spot:
{body}
Write only the finished words that go into the page there, in plain paragraphs (markdown headings, bullets and dividers are fine), with no questions back, no offers and nothing about yourself. Then finish_work with result { "show": [{ "title": "Write", "text": <exactly those words> }] }: the page places that text where they asked.

Write this out as a {format_label} in my own voice, part by part: {about}. The format's parts, in order:
{parts}
Save it to my files, then finish_work with result { "show": [{ "title": "{format_label}", "text": <the whole script, part by part> }] } and where you saved it in the summary, so the script shows where I asked for it.

The person pressed "{label}" on these files in their Trillion files, in the folder {folder}:
{names}
For each file, read what is already known about it (read_file_results: its transcript, summary, facts); for one with nothing known yet, transcribe or summarize it first and record_file_results. Then propose_file_tidy with a short plain title for what each file is and, where it clearly belongs somewhere, the folder to move it into (an existing folder when one fits, list_files), citing in evidence the results each suggestion comes from. Suggest only what those results say. The person accepts or rejects each on their Tidy up screen; nothing moves until they do. finish_work with how many you suggested and any file you could not.

The person pressed "{label}" on the board of the space "{space_title}" (space_id {space_id}) and asked for pictures of: {what}
What is on the board now: {items}
Make them with your own image tools (ChatGPT image generation, Ideogram or any other you can use), a few distinct takes unless they asked for a number. Keep each picture in their Trillion files with write_file, then share each into the space with share_to_space (space_id {space_id}, file): every picture shared into the space appears on its board for everyone in it. Then finish_work with what you made and where.

On the board of the space "{space_title}" (space_id {space_id}) the person chose: {items}
They asked: {what}
Read the space with read_space and any picture with read_shared_file (each "space item" above is an item_id in that space). Do it yourself with your own tools and Trillion's: for a post, draft_post with the picture and words, sent to the accounts it belongs on (list_post_destinations), approved and published as they asked; for anything else, the tools the job needs. Put what you make back in the space with add_to_space or share_to_space, so it shows on the board. Then finish_work with what you did and where it went.
